"<strong>Q4.</strong> While the crystal melts, the temperature holds still but the heater keeps adding heat. Where does the heat go? Use the bond energy readout and the bonds on screen.",
"<strong>Q5.</strong> In the Atoms view, boiling takes about four times the heat per mole of melting. Explain why, using the number of neighbors an atom has in the solid, the liquid and the vapor. What else does the heat do while the sample boils?",
